  "schema": 1,
  "base_commit": "3bebcf79baa2bb72e2ee5ed3897fe843d201eda5",
  "purpose": "Test whether the latency and nominal-byte clock transfers to matched dependent and interleaved operations after its opposite errors on Rust GCD and lower_bound. Keep all rows. Analyze whole-process time.",
  "hypotheses": [
    "Serial and four-chain variants execute the same ordered hot-loop opcodes, instruction counts, operations and nominal operand bytes. Interleaving changes the data dependencies and may change native throughput.",
    "Both DIV input magnitudes use 32-bit unsigned division and the same positive divisor. The congruent addends preserve the divisor and remainder stream. Test whether changing the dividend alone changes native time or modeled latency.",
    "Changing table size at the same hot load count tests address dependence and working-set effects. Cross-size whole-process comparisons also include initialization and page faults. No cache-miss, DRAM or PMU attribution is inferred."
  ],
  "cpu": 1,
  "platform": "Independent private Seoul N2D VM, one thread per core. CPU 1 hosts children, CPU 0 hosts the observer and system services. Fresh instance, production runtime, x86-64-v2 CPUID, REP, latency and operand bytes enabled. Capture placement and verify deletion of VM and boot disk.",
