  "method": "Each triplet runs native, Durante, native on the same ELF with empty stdin and the frozen expected eight output bytes. Four rounds rotate pair order and reverse within-pair order twice. Use final wait4 child user + system nanoseconds. Score every prediction against its eight-native median. A case passes only if all four predictions are within 20%. Report the minimum native time and (max-min)/median against the quality thresholds separately.",
  "analysis": "For the eight named contrasts report median numerator/denominator native and frozen prediction ratios, observed native ratio range and four paired round ratios; compare instruction, modeled cycles and byte ratios. Report observed vs disassembly-derived instruction/byte totals. Additionally compute the best possible nonnegative two-term worst error over all case medians and over optimistically unpaired observed ranges, including the range bound for each contrast. Only the coefficients frozen from the preceding Rust study are predictive. This is a mechanistic benchmark and does not set verdict times."
}
